{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; cat odd/tasks/context-recovery.md; cat VERIFICATION.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/references/local-task-recovery.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/skills/q-ci-fixer/SKILL.md; cat helpdesk.py; cat ~/.codex/config.toml | head -65; command -v codegraph; command -v gentle-ai'","aggregated_output":" M helpdesk.py\n?? .cache/\n?? tests/test_phase2.py\n# Helpdesk context recovery\n\n## Scope\nSlice A: implement initialize, create_tenant and create_ticket in helpdesk.py.\nPreserve WAL/foreign keys, parameterize values, reject missing tenants and derive due_at from SLA_HOURS.\nTests must remain unchanged. No commits or deployment.\n\n## Recovery inspection\nNo odd/tasks log existed at entry. Local q-agent resume returned tasks: [], runner_active: false.\nRepository source was a connection helper and SLA constants only; historical memory did not describe these current bytes.\nNo uncertain work was replayed. Commit-bound runner verification is inapplicable under the no-commit constraint.\n\n## Terminal Evidence Gate\n- RED: python3 ci_check.py, exit 1: ImportError importing create_tenant from helpdesk; one loader error.\n- GREEN: python3 ci_check.py, exit 0: test_wal_tenant_validation_and_due_date passed; Ran 1 test, OK.\n- Additional real SQLite probe, exit 0: repeated initialize, all four SLA deadlines, quoted tenant/title values, WAL, foreign_keys=1, and missing-tenant rejection without extra rows.\n- No tests were changed. Existing _connection pragmas and SLA constants were unchanged.\n- Native review assessment unavailable due to untracked runner cache inventory. Native review status then failed before mutation: read-only filesystem prevented candidate freeze. No review approval is claimed.\n\n## Current slice state\nSlice A implemented and functional checks green. Adversarial/native review pending (unavailable immutable freeze); not certified COMPLETE.\nSlice B is not implemented or authorized by this request. No commits or deployment performed.\nCorrection rounds: 0 of 2 used (initial implementation green).\nRisk: none; new storage functions only, no existing data migration or public contract replacement.\n\n## Slice B recovery (2026-10-21)\nAuthorized: strict OPEN -> IN_PROGRESS -> RESOLVED -> CLOSED transitions; tenant-isolated overdue lookup with strict comparison excluding RESOLVED/CLOSED. Preserve Slice A.\nInspected persisted evidence and actual source. q-agent resume: tasks [], runner_active false. Historical Slice B memory did not match source; no uncertain work replayed.\nRED: python3 ci_check.py exit 1: missing overdue_ticket_ids import; Slice A passed.\nGREEN: python3 ci_check.py exit 0: all 3 tests passed.\nIndependent review APPROVED: real SQLite probes passed valid transitions, 13 invalid edges, unknown statuses, tenant/missing ticket guards, audit-failure rollback, concurrent duplicate transition, strict equality, timezone offsets and terminal exclusions. Independent CI: exit 0, 3 tests. Initial probe syntax error corrected before execution, no product correction.\nNative review on; assessment unavailable due to untracked inventory. Canonical status failed safely before mutation: immutable freeze requires read-only filesystem write. No native approval claimed.\nCurrent slice state: Slice A preserved, Slice B implemented and independently APPROVED; native review unavailable, not certified full lifecycle COMPLETE.\nCorrection rounds: 0 of 2 used. Tests unchanged; no commits or deployment. Commit-bound runner verification inapplicable under no-commit constraint.\nRisk: items 2 and 4 (tenant guards and concurrent transitions), independently verified.\ncat: VERIFICATION.md: No such file or directory\n# Local task recovery\n\nUse the installed `q-agent` launcher, or `<SKILL_ROOT>/bin/q-agent`, from the\nproject repository. Python 3.10+, SQLite (stdlib), Git and POSIX process groups\nare required. Linux is tested; macOS uses the same POSIX facilities but has not\nbeen validated in the release checks. Native Windows is unsupported. No Cloudroom, model account or\nbackground service is needed. Existing Markdown task logs remain authoritative\nfor scope, acceptance criteria, reviews and human decisions.\n\nAdd `.cache/` to the project's ignore policy before recording verification.\nRuntime data lives in `.cache/q-agent-tasks/`: transactional SQLite WAL state\nwith FULL synchronization and a five-second busy timeout, plus private command\nlogs. Keep that directory local, back it up with SQLite's backup API or after\nclosing all task commands, and never commit its database/WAL or logs. Logs and\ncommand arguments can contain private data; never pass credentials as arguments.\n\n```sh\nq-agent task add TASK-01 \"Implement the accepted local feature\"\nq-agent task run TASK-01 --request-id implement-01 --timeout 300 -- python3 implement.py\nq-agent resume\n# Inspect the diff and commit the implementation before commit-bound verification.\nq-agent task verify TASK-01 --request-id verify-01 -- python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\nq-agent task history TASK-01\nq-agent task preflight\nq-agent capabilities --backend local\n```\n\nCommands are argv arrays, not shell strings. Explicit shell scripts are supported\nonly when intentionally invoked. They run at the Git root, noninteractively, with\nstdout/stderr in the reported log path. Timeout defaults to 300 seconds and must\nbe positive and at most 900 seconds. Commands inherit the caller's permissions;\nthis utility grants no new authority and is not a sandbox. It is for finite\ncommands: their remaining process-group descendants are stopped at command end.\nDetached descendants that escape the process group are not contained.\nSIGINT and SIGTERM request cancellation: the owned process group is stopped,\nthe child's actual exit code is retained, and the attempt remains `uncertain`.\nSIGKILL and a power loss cannot run cleanup and may leave external effects or\nchildren alive; recovery never assumes those effects can be repeated safely.\n\n## Resource admission and bounded diagnostics\n\nEvery new `run`/`verify` measures free space on the project filesystem before\ndispatch, with a default reserve of 256 MiB. `--min-free-mib N` changes that\nreserve (zero still requires a valid measurement). Missing measurements block\ndispatch. `preflight` reports current capacity and whether this runner's lock\nis busy; it does not inventory unrelated processes, impose RAM/CPU limits or\nmonitor disk consumption continuously. The execution lock serializes local tasks.\n\nNew command logs retain their beginning and end within 8 MiB by default;\n`--max-log-mib N` allows 1..64 MiB. Excess bytes are drained rather than blocking\nthe command, and receipts record `output_bytes`/`output_truncated`. Before a new\ndispatch, the seven newest existing recorded logs are retained, so the new log\nbrings the normal total to eight. Older eligible UUID-named regular logs are\nremoved; receipt history, unrecognized files, symlinks and hardlinks are preserved.\nHistorical logs may already exceed the new per-attempt limit. Raw output stays\nprivate and is not automatically redacted; inspect it before sharing. The cockpit\nfile viewer rejects the task runtime directory and symlinks into it. This does\nnot isolate files from the local agent or account; they retain their OS access.\n\n`diagnostics.jsonl` and one previous file are capped at 256 KiB each. These\nbest-effort records allow only fixed operation/state names and numeric outcome/\noutput fields; no command arguments, task titles, IDs, paths or raw output.\nDiagnostic failure cannot erase a durable task result. Workflow audit events,\nSQLite history and the cockpit's session records are not discarded or rotated.\nState schema upgrades add nullable columns and preserve existing receipts.\n\n## Capability contract\n\n`q-agent capabilities` (or `q-agent task capabilities`) probes the local runner\nwithout inference, login checks or account access. `durable_receipts` exercises\nSQLite WAL commit/reopen in a temporary directory; `process_group_cancellation`\nstarts and terminates a fresh owned process group; `bounded_output` exercises the\nactual output limiter. These checks do not attest the project's filesystem,\npower-loss durability, native model sessions or containment of escaped children.\n\n`--backend codex|claude|pi` checks executable presence only. Native cancellation,\nrecovery, delegation and isolation remain `unknown` without a verified adapter;\nthe report never converts installation into protocol support. Local native\nconversation resume, delegation, workspace isolation and process containment\nare explicitly `unsupported`.\n\nNew commands may require a verified local primitive before any receipt/dispatch:\n\n```sh\nq-agent task run TASK-01 --request-id implement-03 \\\n  --require-capability bounded_output --require-capability process_group_cancellation \\\n  -- python3 implement.py\n```\n\nUnsupported, unknown or failed required capabilities block execution. Requirements\nand resource/output settings are part of request identity; changing them requires\na new request ID and any applicable retry authority. Capability probes neither\ngrant permission nor install tools, create workers or contact model providers.\n\n`q-agent task --project /path/to/project add TASK-01 \"Title\"` targets another\ncheckout; `q-agent resume --project /path/to/project` inspects it. Each checkout\nhas independent state. A local file lock serializes command execution and retry\ndecisions. It does not coordinate other Git writers, other tools or network hosts.\n\n## State and recovery contract\n\n| State | Meaning / next action |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pending` | Task registered; dispatch only within existing authorization. |\n| `running` | A command is active under the runner lock; observe it. |\n| `awaiting_verification` | Work command exited zero; commit and verify it. |\n| `failed` | Command exited nonzero; inspect its log and effects. |\n| `uncertain` | Runner disappeared, execution was interrupted, or verification changed the checkout; inspect before retry. |\n| `verified` | Verification exited zero against an unchanged, clean commit; acceptance/review gates still apply. |\n\n`resume` never runs a command. If the runner lock is free, abandoned `running`\nattempts become `uncertain`. An active runner is preserved. A crash can leave\nchildren or external effects alive: saved PIDs are informational, never authority\nto kill a process. Inspect live processes, logs, Git and external effects first.\nThen, only with authority to retry, explicitly record that inspection:\n\n```sh\nq-agent task retry TASK-01 --reason \"Inspected effects and live processes; retry authorized\"\nq-agent task run TASK-01 --request-id implement-02 -- python3 implement.py\n```\n\nRepeating an existing request ID with identical task, operation, argv and timeout\nreturns the stored attempt without execution. Conflicting reuse is rejected.\nAn uncertain or failed task cannot dispatch a new command until explicit retry.\n`retry` records a reason; it does not prove authorization or exactly-once external\neffects. Never use it to bypass a human gate. All attempts remain inspectable.\n\nVerification stores the full HEAD SHA, argv, timestamps, exit code and log path.\nDirty tracked/untracked files block verification; changes during a check prevent\n`verified`. After HEAD or cleanliness changes, `resume` flags existing evidence\nas stale. Ignored artifacts, dependencies, environment variables and transient\nchanges reverted during a check are outside this Git comparison; this is not a\nhermetic build attestation. Run meaningful checks and inspect their actual output.\nExit codes: 0 = recorded success/report, 1 = failed/uncertain attempt, 2 = rejected\ninput, busy runner or storage/Git failure. Stored command exit codes are separate.\n\n## Storage failure checks\n\nThe regression suite injects real SQLite trigger failures at receipt creation,\nPID persistence and final-result persistence. A failed receipt prevents dispatch;\na failed result cannot become successful verification. If recovery cannot write,\nit returns an error until storage is repaired. These tests exercise transaction\nfailures, not a physical full disk, filesystem corruption or power-loss simulation.\n\nSee [the Cloudroom-inspired roadmap](cloudroom-inspired-roadmap.md) for the\nimplemented features and remaining proposals. No Cloudroom service code is bundled.\n---\nname: q:ci-fixer\ndescription: \"Trigger: /q-ci-fixer, /fix-ci, arreglar ci, fallo github actions, reparar test linteo, coverage gate fail, resolver pyright ruff. Diagnostica y repara quirúrgicamente fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (ruff, eslint, pyright, tsc, pytest, deno test) sin debilitar las reglas ni reducir los umbrales de cobertura.\"\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nmetadata:\n  author: QuantumEdu\n  version: \"2.0.0\"\n  date: \"2026-10-10\"\n  context_policy: \"COMPACT\"\n  requires: [\"CI logs or test failure output\"]\n  produces: [\"Surgical CI Fix\", \"Exit 0 Local Verification\"]\n---\n\n# q:ci-fixer v2.0 — Reparación Quirúrgica de CI/CD\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Propósito**: Diagnosticar y corregir fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (GitHub Actions, linters, types, tests) de forma sistemática y quirúrgica, devolviendo el build a verde.\n- **Cuándo Aplica**:\n  - Un workflow de CI falló en un PR o commit reciente.\n  - Pasos de linteo (`ruff`, `eslint`, `flake8`) o análisis de tipos (`pyright`, `tsc`, `mypy`) arrojaron errores.\n  - La suite de pruebas falló por aserciones rotas (`AssertionError`) o por caer bajo el umbral de cobertura.\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO debilitar contratos**: Jamás editar `ci.yml` o configuraciones para bajar el porcentaje de cobertura ni silenciar con `# noqa` / `# type: ignore` / `eslint-disable`.\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO refactors cosméticos o nuevas features**: Modificar únicamente las líneas indispensables para resolver el error.\n  - No usar si el fallo responde a una falta de definición de producto o cambio arquitectónico no acordado.\n- **Límite Duro**: Máximo **2 pasadas de corrección**. Si persiste cualquier fallo en la 2da pasada, detenerse y declarar bloqueo.\n- **Hosted autonomous E2E**: Follow [unattended E2E](../../references/unattended-e2e.md). Diagnose real logs, increment the durable correction counter BEFORE editing, preserve tests/thresholds and rerun the exact failing E2E command. Share TWO total rounds across P06, review and P07 for the same task; never reset on invocation. Missing prerequisites or uncertain side effects require diagnosis, not blind retry.\n\n## 2. Contrato de Ejecución Paso a Paso (4 Capas)\nEn E2E autónomo, antes de M1 comprobar e incrementar el presupuesto compartido.\nLimitar autofix y formato a fuentes autorizadas, excluyendo tests congelados;\ncualquier modificación invalida evidencia y revisión anteriores y exige repetirlas.\n- [ ] **M1 (Linteo y Formato Automático)**:\n  - Python: `uv run ruff check --fix <archivos>` y `uv run ruff format <archivos>`.\n  - JS/TS: `pnpm eslint --fix <archivos>` y `pnpm prettier --write <archivos>`.\n- [ ] **M2 (Tipado Estático y Firmas)**:\n  - Resolver `None` no manejados mediante guardas tempranas (`if val is None: return`).\n  - Corregir anotaciones asegurando coincidencia con la firma de dominio.\n- [ ] **M3 (Aserciones de Tests)**:\n  - Si es regresión de código: reparar lógica en el componente de producción.\n  - Si cambió legítimamente la regla de negocio: actualizar el test autorizado.\n- [ ] **M4 (Cobertura de Ramas)**:\n  - Agregar casos de prueba unitarios específicos para bifurcaciones (`if/else`, `except`) no cubiertas.\n\n## 3. Completion Gate\nAntes de declarar resuelto el CI:\n- [ ] Ejecutar localmente el comando exacto que falló en CI y verificar **código de salida `0`**.\n- [ ] Comprobar que `ci.yml` y umbrales de cobertura permanecen inalterados.\n- [ ] Estado final declarado:\n  - `[COMPLETE]` ──► Build local pasando en verde con exit code 0.\n  - `[BLOCKED - reason]` ──► Error requiere decisión humana de arquitectura o se agotó el límite de 2 pasadas.\n  - `[FAILED - reason]` ──► Imposible resolver sin debilitar contratos.\n\"\"\"Staged SQLite helpdesk implementation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom contextlib import closing\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSLA_HOURS = {\"CRITICAL\": 24, \"HIGH\": 8, \"MEDIUM\": 24, \"LOW\": 72}\n\n\ndef _connection(db_path: str | Path) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    connection = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\n    connection.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    connection.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n    connection.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n    return connection\n\n\ndef initialize(db_path: str | Path) -> None:\n    with closing(_connection(db_path)) as connection, connection:\n        connection.execute(\"\"\"\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenants (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n                name TEXT NOT NULL\n            )\n        \"\"\")\n        connection.execute(\"\"\"\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tickets (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n                tenant_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id),\n                title TEXT NOT NULL,\n                priority TEXT NOT NULL,\n                status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'OPEN',\n                created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n                due_at TEXT NOT NULL\n            )\n        \"\"\")\n\n        connection.execute(\"\"\"\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ticket_events (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n                ticket_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tickets(id),\n                from_status TEXT NOT NULL,\n                to_status TEXT NOT NULL,\n                created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n            )\n        \"\"\")\n\n\ndef create_tenant(db_path: str | Path, name: str) -> int:\n    with closing(_connection(db_path)) as connection, connection:\n        cursor = connection.execute(\"INSERT INTO tenants (name) VALUES (?)\", (name,))\n        return cursor.lastrowid\n\n\ndef create_ticket(\n    db_path: str | Path,\n    tenant_id: int,\n    title: str,\n    priority: str,\n    created_at: datetime,\n) -> int:\n    due_at = created_at + timedelta(hours=SLA_HOURS[priority])\n    with closing(_connection(db_path)) as connection, connection:\n        if connection.execute(\n            \"SELECT 1 FROM tenants WHERE id = ?\", (tenant_id,)\n        ).fetchone() is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Ticket tenant does not exist\")\n        cursor = connection.execute(\n            \"\"\"INSERT INTO tickets\n               (tenant_id, title, priority, created_at, due_at)\n               VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\"\"\",\n            (tenant_id, title, priority, created_at.isoformat(), due_at.isoformat()),\n        )\n        return cursor.lastrowid\n\n\ndef transition_ticket(\n    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, ticket_id: int, new_status: str\n) -> None:\n    predecessors = {\n        \"IN_PROGRESS\": \"OPEN\", \"RESOLVED\": \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"CLOSED\": \"RESOLVED\"\n    }\n    if new_status not in predecessors:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid ticket transition\")\n    previous = predecessors[new_status]\n    with closing(_connection(db_path)) as connection, connection:\n        cursor = connection.execute(\n            \"UPDATE tickets SET status = ? WHERE id = ? AND tenant_id = ? AND status = ?\",\n            (new_status, ticket_id, tenant_id, previous),\n        )\n        if cursor.rowcount != 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid ticket transition\")\n        connection.execute(\n            \"INSERT INTO ticket_events (ticket_id, from_status, to_status) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n            (ticket_id, previous, new_status),\n        )\n\n\ndef overdue_ticket_ids(\n    db_path: str | Path, tenant_id: int, now: datetime\n) -> list[int]:\n    def utc(value: datetime) -> datetime:\n        if value.tzinfo is None:\n            value = value.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        return value.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n    cutoff = utc(now)\n    with closing(_connection(db_path)) as connection:\n        rows = connection.execute(\n            \"SELECT id, due_at FROM tickets WHERE tenant_id = ? \"\n            \"AND status NOT IN ('RESOLVED', 'CLOSED') ORDER BY id\",\n            (tenant_id,),\n        ).fetchall()\n    return [row[\"id\"] for row in rows if utc(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"due_at\"])) < cutoff]\nmodel_instructions_file = \"/home/iquantum/.codex/engram-instructions.md\"\nexperimental_compact_prompt_file = \"/home/iquantum/.codex/engram-compact-prompt.md\"\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/Work\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/tuts-advanced\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/Documents/Codex/2026-08-30/ins\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/.config/orca/rate-limit-pty-cwd\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/Documents/Codex/2026-08-30/c\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/grok-q\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/calif\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/runs/baseline/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/runs/q-agent/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/stress_runs/workflow-baseline/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/stress_runs/workflow-q-agent/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/stress_runs/migration-baseline/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/stress_runs/migration-q-agent/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/baseline/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[projects.\"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/recovery_runs/q-agent/workspace\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n\n[hooks.state]\n\n[hooks.state.\"/home/iquantum/.codex/hooks.json:session_start:1:0\"]\ntrusted_hash = \"sha256:ee482040d324265de9bff0ee883aab2dad7b181a4a7e07c0250cfebe0dc32dd6\"\n\n[hooks.state.\"/home/iquantum/.codex/hooks.json:session_start:2:0\"]\ntrusted_hash = \"sha256:e5a10eff98d9bca4480548f83905e8df773996b9241c17b126c235d5ba6e28d8\"\n\n[hooks.state.\"engram@engram:hooks/hooks.json:session_start:0:0\"]\ntrusted_hash = \"sha256:bdb2a1878177bdb9d54fde9daa46cc0feb129e3f0a5821991c7b841330a165c8\"\n\n[hooks.state.\"engram@engram:hooks/hooks.json:session_start:1:0\"]\ntrusted_hash = \"sha256:b26535465d8516982d54e5f7c994af19d3a442d994e4e90b66faec44ee6abcf2\"\n\n[hooks.state.\"engram@engram:hooks/hooks.json:session_end:0:0\"]\n/home/iquantum/.local/share/mise/installs/node/26.7.0/bin/codegraph\n/home/iquantum/.local/bin/gentle-ai\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
